WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.460
We are here with Sharon Chuter, the founder of UOMA Beauty

2
00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:06.230
a company that I have been a huge fan of

3
00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:07.430
for a really long time.

4
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:09.230
I can't believe I'm doing the show with you Sharon.

5
00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:11.730
And we have another connection, which was

6
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.623
that I was lucky enough to participate in your

7
00:00:13.623 --> 00:00:15.930
pull-up for change.

8
00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:17.610
Yes you did.

9
00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:20.450
Thank you for allowing me to that party.

10
00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:23.810
Everybody jumped on board because your mission was so clear.

11
00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:27.590
Why did you start the pull-up for change hashtag?

12
00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:30.980
Yes, I did that really to drive, or raise more awareness,

13
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:33.356
or shine more light to the lack of economic opportunities

14
00:00:33.356 --> 00:00:36.571 line:15%
for the black community, especially within the beauty space.

15
00:00:36.571 --> 00:00:38.673 line:15%
I know we've been talking about lack of inclusivity

16
00:00:38.673 --> 00:00:40.241 line:15%
but it was really to shine light

17
00:00:40.241 --> 00:00:41.898 line:15%
at some of the root causes of this,

18
00:00:41.898 --> 00:00:44.816 line:15%
because really it's like, it's like a computer, right?

19
00:00:44.816 --> 00:00:46.554
Whatever you put in it's what's gonna come out.

20
00:00:46.554 --> 00:00:48.663
And so for me, that was really the driver

21
00:00:48.663 --> 00:00:50.730
to make sure that we have a better world

22
00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.449
where we have more economic equality

23
00:00:52.449 --> 00:00:55.560
because the economic inequality in America right now

24
00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:56.399
is at pandemic level.

25
00:00:56.399 --> 00:00:58.629
So thank you for participating and pulling up.

26
00:00:58.629 --> 00:01:00.426
Were you always such an activist?

27
00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:02.807
Because your activism is so strong and powerful

28
00:01:02.807 --> 00:01:05.700
and a real game changer in the industry now.

29
00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.090
Were you always that person

30
00:01:07.090 --> 00:01:10.250
or did you have a tidal wave of inspiration?

31
00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.050
Well for me, I've always been the person

32
00:01:12.050 --> 00:01:13.130
who speaks up, you know?

33
00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:15.160 line:15%
In my country we call it (mumbles), right.

34
00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:16.070 line:15%
Speak louder.

35
00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.520 line:15%
So I've always been that troublemaker.

36
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.070 line:15%
As a kid I would get beat up all the time.

37
00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:21.010 line:15%
So I think from mine, I didn't even know

38
00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:21.890 line:15%
that was a word for it.

39
00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:25.018 line:15%
It's just whenever I see something that needs to change

40
00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:27.240
I don't have any means to just sit it out.

41
00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.457
And I think as people, and especially as artists,

42
00:01:30.457 --> 00:01:32.410
as business people, we have,

43
00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:34.550
everything we do have to be connected

44
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:35.860
to the times that we live in.

45
00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.918
And right now we live in times of gross injustice.

46
00:01:37.918 --> 00:01:41.040
So for me, it would be just odd, just go in your bag,

47
00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.189
you know, selling lipsticks and eyeliners

48
00:01:43.189 --> 00:01:46.522
and yay, people are dying and starving and you know,

49
00:01:46.522 --> 00:01:49.010
there's injustice and it's like, oh, who cares?

50
00:01:49.010 --> 00:01:50.717
I just wanna wear makeup, you know?

51
00:01:50.717 --> 00:01:53.170
So, so I think that, there was no option you know?

52
00:01:53.170 --> 00:01:54.880
Sharon, I feel the exact same way.

53
00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:56.810
I try to be so positive on this show,

54
00:01:56.810 --> 00:01:59.700
but I wanna talk about the pain and the reality

55
00:01:59.700 --> 00:02:02.600
and the world we are living in.

56
00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.594
And unless I'm living in reality

57
00:02:04.594 --> 00:02:07.360
then I don't feel like I have the right to be positive.

58
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.730
So I really understand that side.

59
00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:13.530
And 2020 in my opinion has been

60
00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.630
one of the most important years in history, period.

61
00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:17.463
Yes.
(lady laughing)

62
00:02:17.463 --> 00:02:18.900
And I'm honored to be a part of it

63
00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.788
and have been woken up and learned

64
00:02:20.788 --> 00:02:22.755
and everything that you've done for it.

65
00:02:22.755 --> 00:02:26.246
And on a completely beauty junkie level

66
00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:30.974
that has nothing to do with the crucial and vital activism

67
00:02:30.974 --> 00:02:34.390
that you do, and that we're all learning from,

68
00:02:34.390 --> 00:02:37.400
which is your beauty brand is one of my favorites.

69
00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:38.755
It's just an amazing beauty (mumbles).

70
00:02:38.755 --> 00:02:40.840
I love it, it's extraordinary.

71
00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:41.943
Your products, your packaging.

72
00:02:41.943 --> 00:02:43.510
It's like my favorite.

73
00:02:43.510 --> 00:02:44.866
I was so excited to have you on the show

74
00:02:44.866 --> 00:02:47.017
go to our website at thedrewbarrymoreshow.com

75
00:02:47.017 --> 00:02:51.440
to look more at Sharon's important work

76
00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:52.834
in beauty and activism.

77
00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:55.469
Sharon, thank you for coming on this show.

78
00:02:55.469 --> 00:02:56.302
Thank you so much.

79
00:02:56.302 --> 00:02:57.135
I'm such a huge fan of yours.

80
00:02:57.135 --> 00:02:59.802 line:15%
(upbeat music)

